Add({
	id = "blackfathom-deeps",
	title = "Blackfathom Deeps",
	aliases = { "Blackfathom" },
	parent = "ashenvale",
	continent = "Kalimdor",
	zone = "Blackfathom Deeps",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
	},
	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Blackfathom Deeps is a drowned temple beneath the coast of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}, on the {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram Strand{/link}. A shaft lined with old stairs falls from the shore into dark water, and the way in must be swum. Beyond it lie flooded caverns, broken shrines and sunken halls of pale elven stone. Once this was a holy place of the moon goddess Elune. Now it belongs to the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link}, to the {link:naga}naga{/link} and the {link:satyrs}satyrs{/link} who serve beside them, and to the thing they worship in the deepest pool: the hydra {link:aku-mai}Aku'mai{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[In the age before the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} raised a great temple to Elune on the western shore of ancient {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. It is written that {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} herself oversaw its building. At its heart lay a moonwell. When the Sundering tore the world apart, the temple broke and sank beneath the waves, and for ages it lay lost and silent. Even then it did not keep only holy things. An elf named Lorgalis, a worshipper of the {red:old-gods}Old Gods{/red}, left a manuscript of their praise within its walls, and it was never destroyed.

In later days, a corruption of the Old Gods seeped up from beneath the earth and fouled the sacred moonwell. {link:aku-mai}Aku'mai{/link}, a servant of those ancient powers, rose from the waters and made the ruins her lair.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} has come to the Deeps to worship the hydra. Its cultists are of many peoples, humans and orcs, trolls, {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and even {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}, all bound together by their faith in the return of the Old Gods. Led by {link:twilight-lord-kelris}Twilight Lord Kelris{/link}, they offer innocents to {link:aku-mai}Aku'mai{/link} in exchange for power. The {link:naga}naga{/link} of the Blackfathom tribe have joined them, and satyrs of the Fallenroot haunt the tunnels. The naga harvest sapphires from the cave walls, for the spirits of water cling to those stones.

The world above has taken notice. The {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} in {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} sent a scout to watch the temple, and he did not return. The {link:earthen-ring}Earthen Ring{/link} sent the troll {link:je-neu-sancrea}Je'neu Sancrea{/link} to the {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram Strand{/link} to learn what the cult is doing to the elements. {link:gershala-nightwhisper}Gershala Nightwhisper{/link} of {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link} wants the brains of the corrupted naga and satyrs for her studies, and {red:gerrig-bonegrip}Gerrig Bonegrip{/red} of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} covets the manuscript of Lorgalis.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Deeps",
			text = [=[• {b}The Drowned Entrance.{/b} Stairs and flooded passages lead down from the shore. Sapphire clusters glitter on the walls, and {link:naga}naga{/link} priestesses gather them.
• {b}The Pool of Ask'ar.{/b} A great flooded cave with an island at its centre, where the maddened turtle {link:ghamoo-ra}Ghamoo-ra{/link} roams. The wounded scout {link:argent-guard-thaelrid}Thaelrid{/link} hides near it. In a side cove the sea witch {link:lady-sarevess}Lady Sarevess{/link} keeps her own court.
• {b}The Shrine of {link:gelihast}Gelihast{/link}.{/b} Blindlight murlocs gather here around their chief and his altar.
• {b}The Moonshrine Ruins.{/b} The broken halls of the old temple, half under water, where the cultists hold their camps. A fathom stone lies in the water, and something elemental guards it.
• {b}The Forgotten Pool.{/b} Beneath the ruins, a drowned cave where an ancient thresher has never been caught.
• {b}The Moonshrine Sanctum.{/b} Here {link:twilight-lord-kelris}Twilight Lord Kelris{/link} sits in trance before the altar of the Old Gods.
• {b}{link:aku-mai}Aku'mai{/link}'s Lair.{/b} Past the sealed doors of the sanctum lies the deepest pool, where the hydra waits.]=],
		},
	},
})

